$\begin{align}
g'(x)&=\dfrac{d}{dx}\left[ \dfrac{x^2-3}{x+2} \right]
\\\\
&=\dfrac{\dfrac{d}{dx}[x^2-3](x+2)-(x^2-3)\dfrac{d}{dx}[x+2]}{(x+2)^2}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{(2x)(x+2)-(x^2-3)(1)}{(x+2)^2}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{x^2+4x+3}{(x+2)^2}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{(x+1)(x+3)}{(x+2)^2}
\end{align}$

Now let's look for $x$-values where $g'$ is zero or undefined.
